            <div xml:id="d29-a2">

                <pb facs="0118" n="60" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg60"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 2.</seg></opener>
                <head>[Translation.]</head>
                <p rendition="#center">DEPARTMENT OF FOREIGN RELATIONS AND GOVERNMENT, OFFICE OF
                    GOVERNMENT— SECTION FIRST.</p>
                <p>The citizen President of the republic left the city of Chihuahua the 9th, and
                    arrived here yesterday, where he has determined to fix the seat of the national
                    government, for the time being.</p>
                <p>It is unnecessary to repeat that the citizen President of the republic will
                    always firmly maintain his resolution to sustain the cause of the independence
                    and institutions of the republic, under all the vicissitudes of war, which are
                    now decreasing, and the enemy’s resources will soon be exhausted by the constant
                    struggle of the Mexican people, who are bound to triumph at no very distant
                    period.</p>
                <p>Independence and liberty! Paso del Norte, December 19, 1865.</p>
                <p rendition="#right">LERDO DE TEJADA.</p>
                <p>The Citizen <hi rendition="#small-caps">Governor <hi rendition="#italic">of the
                            State of</hi>——</hi>.</p>
                <p>A true copy:</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JUAN VALDES, <hi rendition="#italic">First
                        Officer.</hi></signed><lb/><dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi
                                rendition="#small-caps">Paso del Norte</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1865-12-19"><hi rendition="#italic"><hi
                                    rendition="#small-caps">December</hi></hi> 19,
                        1865</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
